{
  "_comment": "Answers derived by hand (reachable markings listed per net, written as vectors over p0..). Q0 edges = pairs (marking, transition enabled there). Q6 is read literally: some place has the same token count in every reachable marking (a never-marked place counts, with 0). For unbounded nets Q1/Q3/Q4 are out of the evaluation scope (SPEC 3) but are decidable here by the explicit reachable family and are given. Targets: marking = token counts per place index; the same marking may appear as QR and QC to separate reachable from coverable.",
  "cal-01-circuit-live": {
    "reachable": "(1,0,0) (0,1,0) (0,0,1): the single token walks the ring",
